$voice_enhance — Resemble Enhance on vocal stems (sounds[])



SUMMARY

  Denoises and enhances each sound in sounds[] using Resemble Enhance
  (resemble-ai/resemble-enhance). Typical use: clean vocals after $music_separation.



SYNTAX

  $voice_enhance
  $voice_enhance(device=cuda)
  $voice_enhance(denoise_only=1)
  $voice_enhance(denoise_before=1, device=cuda, nfe=64)



INPUT

  sounds[] — required; WAV/MP3 vocal tracks.



OUTPUT

  sounds[] — one enhanced WAV per input ({timestamp}_{index}_enhanced.wav).



ARGUMENTS

  device= — cuda, cpu, or auto (default: auto).

  denoise_only= — run denoiser only, skip enhancer (0/1).

  denoise_before= — denoise then enhance (0/1).

  nfe= — CFM steps, 1–128 (default 64).

  solver= — midpoint, rk4, or euler (default midpoint).

  lambd= — CFM prior weight 0–1 (default 0.5).

  tau= — CFM temperature 0–1 (default 0.5).



MODELS

  models/resemble-enhance/enhancer_stage2/ — downloaded from ResembleAI/resemble-enhance on first use.

  AH_RESEMBLE_ENHANCE_DIR= — override model root.

  AH_RESEMBLE_ENHANCE_RUN_DIR= — override enhancer_stage2 path.



REQUIREMENTS

  resemble-enhance + torch 2.1.1 in .venvs/voice_enhance (Python 3.11; deepspeed stubbed, Windows PosixPath YAML fix).

  Setup: powershell -File tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1



ENVIRONMENT

  AH_EMULATE_VOICE_ENHANCE=1 — stub files without resemble-enhance.



EXAMPLE

  @vocals: @track -> $music_separation(model=2stem) -> $select(sounds=[0])
  @clean: @vocals -> $voice_enhance(device=cuda)



PROMPT-CONSUMING

  No.
